# Third-party notices — native Qwen3.8-27B executor

## Code reused from this repository

`safetensors_mmap.*`, `tokenizer.*`, `unicode_ranges.hpp`, `image_preprocess.*`,
`stb_image.h`, `bf16.hpp`, `qwen38_gemm.cu` and several elementwise kernels in
`qwen38_kernels.cu` are derived from `native/omni/` in the same repository
(Apache-2.0). The tensor-core GEMM/GEMV code originated there; the hybrid
attention, partial-mRoPE, gated delta rule, depthwise causal conv and vision
merger paths were written for this model.

`stb_image.h` is Sean Barrett's stb_image, public domain / MIT.

`unicode_ranges.hpp` is generated range data for the Unicode general
categories used by the Qwen2 pretokenizer (see
`native/omni_tests/gen_unicode_ranges.py`).

## Specifications implemented from upstream (read, not copied)

- HuggingFace Transformers 5.x, Apache-2.0:
  `src/transformers/models/qwen3_5/modeling_qwen3_5.py`,
  `configuration_qwen3_5.py`, `vision_utils.py`,
  `image_processing_qwen2_vl.py`, `processing_qwen3_vl.py`, and the model's
  `chat_template.jinja`. Formulas, tensor layouts, rounding order and the
  prompt/position-id construction follow these sources.
- Qwen3.8-27B checkpoint (`Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B`, Apache-2.0): weight names,
  shapes and configuration.

## Not used

No vLLM, SGLang, FLA, flash-linear-attention, cuBLAS, cuDNN, PyTorch or
Triton code is linked or copied into this directory. The only runtime
dependency is the NVIDIA CUDA runtime (`libcudart`).
